message: "If you use this software, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "AI Decision System: replayable decision records for AI-assisted go/no-go decisions"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Bicheng
repository-code: "https://github.com/BichengWang/ai-decision-system"
license: MIT
# The repository holds independently versioned components. Version, commit and date
# identify the GitHub releases of expgate, jevdecision and decisioncontrol: all three
# 0.1.0 tags (experiment-gate/v0.1.0, jev-decision/v0.1.0, decision-control/v0.1.0)
# point at this commit and were released on 2026-10-13. RELIA is not released and
# is not covered by this version; the src/ workbench is unversioned.
version: "0.1.0"
commit: 2cadb8b061dc0fa0d79bd0bed7e351da93ea7c1e
date-released: "2026-10-13"
abstract: >-
  This repository develops independent tools for replayable decision records
  for AI-assisted go/no-go decisions, with offline verification of recorded
  evidence. Examples and fixtures demonstrate software behavior rather than
  live-model performance or production adoption. RELIA remains unreleased under
  a separate human-gated process, alongside an unsupported research workbench.
keywords:
  - decision records
  - offline verification
  - replayability
  - AI-assisted decisions
  - go/no-go decisions
